arm64: dts: h713: one tree for the HY200 QZ713DF A1, the HY310's tree under its own name

Two names were wrong. sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts held the HY310's
hardware description: 0024 wrote it for cstenger's bench board, and 0024c,
0064, 0082, 0142, 0157, 0158 and 0162 fitted it to the HY310 (cpu_comm,
console, codec, fan PH17, focus motor, bootargs, accelerometer) while the HY310
included it under its own name (0160). And the HY200 QZ713DF A1 itself - the
silkscreen of the bench board, of the 2025 "HY300 Pro+" and of the
maintainer's HY300PRO-G-EU (read off the board, 02.10.2026) - had its measured
tree under a box label, sun50i-h713-hy300pro-g-eu.dts (0167).

- sun50i-h713-hy310.dts takes the HY310's description from the hy200 file as
  it was, with the HY310's model and compatible in place of the bench
  board's (and the three German comments in English). Its DTB compiles to
  the same bytes as before (host cpp + dtc, the way kbuild does).
- sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts includes sun50i-h713-hy310.dts instead of the
  hy200 file, which held the same nodes; its DTB is byte-identical too.
- sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts becomes 0167's tree: the HY310 include
  plus the lamp's PWM words <5 1 40000 1 1 100>, no pwm-backlight, fan
  tacho PH13, no focus motor, the accelerometer node kept - with model
  "HY200 QZ713DF_A1 (Allwinner H713)" (the model of the board's U-Boot tree)
  and compatible "magcubic,hy200-qz713df-a1". Its DTB is 0167's DTB but
  those two strings.
- sun50i-h713-hy300pro-g-eu.dts and its Makefile line go.

One tree serves both stock firmwares of the board: their vendor_boot device
trees (the 2025-05 one from the HY300PRO-G-EU's eMMC dump, the 2025-09 one
from its update.img) are identical but for motor_ctr, both panel_config.ini
copies of both declare the same [PWMSetting] and ColorDepth 8, and what does
differ - the DRAM clock - is U-Boot's (boards/hy200-qz713df-a1, variants).
The 2025-09 firmware drives a focus motor with the HY310's step tables; the
tree keeps it off, because the HY300PRO-G-EU has none and the driver homes at
probe on PH4..PH7. h713-tv's board_of_dt row follows the new compatible.

Old patches are left as they are; this one sits at the end of the series.
